+This distinction shows why nounhood and fusion are compatible. Ordinary headedness follows here from the proposed projection rules; it doesn't require eliminating every fused construction containing a noun. I retain \textit{CGEL}'s fusion analysis for anaphoric independent genitives such as \mention{mine}, while assigning ordinary Head to independent determinatives such as \mention{few}.
 
